analyses.2:
Only the dihedral-frame family scored above 0. The frame mixture (r1c1) reached 0.209 dev with 0.142 training success, and the frames × corners union (r1c6) reached 0.049. Corner, flattening order and type permutation, alone or with a transpose, all scored 0. The two identity+transpose designs (r1c2, r1c5) also scored 0. That hints the hidden change is a flip-type frame, but seed noise is large, so the evidence is weak. In r1c1, dev success is above training success and both are still low, so the layout probably matches. Undertraining is the more likely limit than generalisation. The program therefore points to one-change optimisation variants of r1c1:
- lr 1.5e-3;
- the 2-epoch recipe;
- the 1-epoch long-rollout recipe;
- 64 minibatches;
- a slimmer frame head, which brings r to about 1 and gives 33% more samples;
- one stacked bet: slim head plus 2 epochs, to maximise samples per FLOP.
All keep 8 learnable frames, because we cannot see which frame r1c1 committed to.
